WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.825
Mastery Starter 12.0.

00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:04.890
New to Operate as Your Own Bank?

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:05.950
Start here.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.037
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:09.730
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.759
A bank keeps assets safe, lends, borrows and

00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:16.060
always has cash for what it owes.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.013
With DeFi you can run those four

00:00:18.013 --> 00:00:21.209
jobs yourself, with written policies, because there's

00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:23.635
nobody to call when something goes wrong.

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:28.170
Balance sheet: assets, liabilities and equity.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.658
Liquidity ladder: reserves tiered by how

00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:32.475
fast you can access them.

00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:36.035
Credit line: borrowing against assets under a policy.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.530
Runway: months your reserve can cover.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.725
Succession: how others recover your assets if you can't.

00:00:43.025 --> 00:00:44.840
Modules 0–11.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.983
Fill in the balance sheet worksheet (W6)

00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:51.965
with rough numbers: equity, LTV and runway.

00:00:53.265 --> 00:00:55.011
Beginner: Has a balance sheet

00:00:55.011 --> 00:00:56.825
and a basic custody split.

00:00:56.825 --> 00:01:01.745
Practitioner: Runs written custody, credit, ladder and lending policies.

00:01:01.745 --> 00:01:04.554
Master: Operates a complete bank with books,

00:01:04.554 --> 00:01:07.799
tax-ready records, succession and quarterly reviews.

00:01:09.099 --> 00:01:11.599
You've mastered this module when a stranger

00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:13.758
could run your bank from your written

00:01:13.758 --> 00:01:15.974
policies, with no keys in any document.

00:01:17.274 --> 00:01:19.789
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:22.654
Next up, Lesson 12.1: Your balance sheet.
